  "reroute_reason": {
   "kind": "rtl_change",
   "reason": "Legacy s3/s4 sources fail the native driver census (max 399) and the Codex s5 structural copy keeps a 3-deep unchanged payload flop delay line (SAFE 5, c1e5bec49). KV-GRP6 s6 (Codex s5 storage audit c1e5bec49): the 1024-b response payload passed four unchanged flop captures (PC out e0 -> hop e1 -> idata e2 -> exit e3; the middle three a >= 3-deep delay line, SAFE 5).  s6: per PC branch the payload delay is a genuine SRAM ring (8 x 4x32 1R1W macros, write slot wp at e1, read the previous slot at e2, exit copies at e3; unreset self-phasing pointers, read != write slot), payload cleared exactly as the old hop cleared it; metadata keeps its hop; two kept exit copies on both tiles; +0 cycles. Gated source = bounded-driver structural copy (max 32) of the mapped s6 RTL."
  },
